      "id": 1,
      "text": "Becker was platted in 1867 and named for state legislator George Loomis Becker.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Becker%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s post office began as Pleasant Valley in 1866, changed to Becker in 1870, and the town grew around a Great Northern Railway station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lakesnwoods.com/Becker.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Sherburne County Generating Station, owned by Xcel Energy, is the largest coal‑fired power plant in Minnesota and supplies about two‑thirds of Becker’s tax revenue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        11,
        12,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Becker%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In February 2024 Microsoft purchased 300 acres that had been earmarked for a Google data center, signaling a new tech presence in Becker.",
